Update design of Operation block types and blocks to operations parser correspondingly.

Input method per blocks types:
1. for 'Rounding', input method is table with columns: Pass, Size, Feed, Angle, Rotations per Feed, Speed.
2. for other operation types input method is unformatted multi-line editable text field.

Design requirements:

1. Text inpu field must have dynamic height. Default height is 1 text line. Height increases automatically based on number of text lines. User can freely input text with line breaks.

Parsing rules for text input fields:
1. Line breaks, tabs and muliple spaces are allowed. They are NOT semantic separators. They serve as old style visual formating tools used by a user. Save text with them as is.
2. The text represents zero, one or multiple operations in specific format separated by one of separators.
3. The only separator is Right arrow. But specific representation of right arrow may differ. It may be '->', '-->' and one of special right arrow symbols predefined in font collections supplied by popular text and tables editors, for example Microsoft Word and Excell. So the user may just copy-paste the text from such an Editor. Brainstorm which Right arrow symbols may be potentially used and register them all as allowed separators.
4. Block's text input fields do auto format of Right arrows in same moment a user input it. Substitute any allowed Right arrow separator into a standard Right arrow symbol. Brainstorm which Right arrow symbol has the best compatibility in case a user copy-paste text form a Block into other editor.
5. For parsing copy full text input as a single string, remove line breaks and tabs, substitute multiple spaces by one space. Split into 'sentences' using arrow separators. For every 'sentence' remove leading and trailing spaces.
6. Each parsed 'sentence' must be classified as one of:"initial_state", "operation" or "unknown".
7. Initial state 'sentence' may be in 1st position only. Initial state format is a real or integer number in round brackets like '(500)'. It represents initial size (height specifically). Must not be treated as an operation.
8. Operation 'sentence' is any 'sentence' that is not initial state with one of predefined format. It must be interpreted as an operation. Examples: '450', '(90) 450', '(90)450', '1', '0', '0(3)', '(45) 450 (3)', '(45)450 (3)', '(45)450(3)'. Below are all inclusive formats, variables and corresponding operation types.
9. Parent block - 'Deforamtion' should have new parameters, edited by user: deformation_variables.tail_chamfering_stroke (decimal); deformation_variables.tail_flattening_stroke (decimal). These variables are inherited by child 'Operation' blocks and may used it to calculate operation's parameters.
